{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789759438,"nonce":"yDG8KqUSsJYLaSFXxKz9CTY0gcE=","message":"Plan, on the owner's direction that the integration point is HIR so any Zyntax frontend (zyn grammars, zyntax_python/zypy, zynml — all consumers of zyntax_embed) is served without friction:\n\n- caribou-zyntax owns one zyntax_embed TieredRuntime per registered language (one LangId per frontend/snapshot). Its unit of work is a HirModule: publish the module's non-external functions from HirFunctionSignature (HirType → TypeRef), compile it with compile_module, call through call_function with a NativeSignature derived from the same HIR. Frontends hand HIR (or a TypedProgram the runtime lowers — zypy's register_runtime + lowering context lives in the runtime, so a public lower-to-HIR on the embed side may be wanted later, zyntax's tracker).\n- Increment 1: grammar frontends. A .zyn under a root is a language named by its @language, its file_extensions name its modules under the roots (game/scorer.zig → namespace game, module scorer, as Wren's are found); the loader parses (LanguageGrammar::parse_with_filename), compile_to_hir + krio passes, compile_module, publishes a class named after the module whose statics are its functions; calls cross as Callable::Dynamic through a core function object (Value → ZyntaxValue → call_function → Value), scalars, bool, void, strings. Wren reaches it by the ordinary import; Haxe next (describe for the macro).\n- Memory in increment 1: zyntax's own class-sized pool with Collector::None (insert_free covers what the analysis proves dead; the rest stays). The conservative MarkSweep assumes one mutator thread and its own stacks, which caribou's tasks break. The core-heap strategy (a descriptor word, allocation from the core, escaping values traced by the core) is item 1 of this issue and a zyntax-side seam.\n- Dependency: zyntax pinned to the pushed rev with a [patch] to ../zyntax while the local tree is ahead (205 files, owner's work in progress), per the runtimes' rule.\n- Later increments in this issue's order: per-fiber handlers, Tasks, effects through the bridge, TypeMeta ↔ TypeDesc, zrtl loader on caribou_abi.","files":null}]}